
-- Batch 6: European recipes + Americas + Oceania + Global
UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Bacon-Wrapped Dates are a popular Spanish tapa that combines the sweetness of Medjool dates with salty, crispy bacon. This flavor combination reflects Spain''s Moorish culinary legacy where dates were introduced during the 8th century Islamic conquest, blended with the Iberian tradition of cured pork products.' WHERE slug = 'bacon-wrapped-dates-es';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Spanish Garlic Shrimp (Gambas al Ajillo) is a classic tapa from Spain, featuring shrimp sizzling in olive oil, garlic, and chili flakes. This dish showcases the Spanish passion for simple, high-quality ingredients and the Mediterranean tradition of olive oil cooking that dates back thousands of years.' WHERE slug = 'spanish-garlic-shrimp-es';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Crème Brûlée is a classic French dessert of rich custard topped with a caramelized sugar crust. Its origins are debated between France, England, and Spain, with the earliest known recipe appearing in a 1691 French cookbook. The dramatic torching of the sugar top has made it a symbol of French culinary elegance.' WHERE slug = 'creme-brulee-fr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Ratatouille is a traditional Provençal vegetable stew from Nice, France, dating to the 18th century. The name comes from "touiller" meaning "to stir up." Originally a humble peasant dish, it gained global fame through the 2007 Pixar film and represents the French Mediterranean philosophy of celebrating seasonal vegetables.' WHERE slug = 'ratatouille-fr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Stuffed Mushrooms with Goat Cheese reflect the French tradition of farcis (stuffed vegetables) dating back centuries in Provençal cuisine. The combination of earthy mushrooms with tangy goat cheese showcases France''s artisan cheese heritage—France produces over 1,000 distinct cheese varieties.' WHERE slug = 'stuffed-mushrooms-fr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Mediterranean Quinoa Salad combines ancient Greek culinary traditions with quinoa, an Andean superfood. While quinoa is South American, this preparation reflects the Greek Mediterranean diet—recognized by UNESCO as an Intangible Cultural Heritage—emphasizing olive oil, fresh vegetables, and herbs.' WHERE slug = 'mediterranean-quinoa-salad-gr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Spanakopita is a beloved Greek spinach and feta pie wrapped in flaky phyllo pastry. The dish has roots in the Byzantine Empire and represents the Greek mastery of phyllo dough, which dates back to at least the 3rd century BCE. Spanakopita is a staple of Greek home cooking and festive occasions.' WHERE slug = 'spanakopita-bites-gr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Tzatziki is a classic Greek condiment of yogurt, cucumber, garlic, and olive oil. Its origins trace to the Persian "mast-o-khiar" but it became quintessentially Greek. Tzatziki embodies the Mediterranean philosophy of simple, fresh ingredients and has been a cornerstone of Greek mezze culture for centuries.' WHERE slug = 'tzatziki-pita-gr';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Mediterranean White Beans and Greens reflects the ancient Greek tradition of cooking dried legumes with seasonal vegetables and olive oil. This style of cooking, part of the UNESCO-recognized Mediterranean diet, has sustained Greek communities for millennia and represents one of the world''s healthiest culinary traditions.' WHERE slug = 'mediterranean-white-beans-greens';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Sheet-Pan Chicken Souvlaki is a modern take on the ancient Greek tradition of grilled meat on skewers. The word "souvlaki" comes from "souvla" meaning spit or skewer. Archaeological evidence shows Greeks have been grilling meat on skewers since at least the Bronze Age (1600 BCE).' WHERE slug = 'sheet-pan-chicken-souvlaki';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Caprese Skewers showcase the Italian Caprese salad tradition from the island of Capri. The combination of fresh mozzarella, tomatoes, and basil represents the colors of the Italian flag and celebrates Italy''s Buffalo mozzarella tradition dating to the 12th century.' WHERE slug = 'caprese-skewers-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Italian Arancini are Sicilian rice balls stuffed with ragù, mozzarella, and peas, then breaded and deep-fried. Dating to the 10th century Arab rule of Sicily, arancini (meaning "little oranges") were originally a way to make rice portable. They remain Sicily''s most iconic street food.' WHERE slug = 'italian-arancini-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Hummus with Pita is one of the world''s oldest prepared foods, with origins dating back over 7,000 years in the Middle East. Made from chickpeas, tahini, lemon, and garlic, hummus is claimed by Lebanon, Israel, Palestine, and Syria. It represents the shared culinary heritage of the Levant.' WHERE slug = 'hummus-pita-lb';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Buffalo Cauliflower Wings are a modern vegetarian twist on Buffalo wings, which were invented in 1964 at the Anchor Bar in Buffalo, New York. This plant-based version emerged in the 2010s health food movement and represents America''s growing interest in vegetable-forward cooking.' WHERE slug = 'buffalo-cauliflower-wings-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Loaded Sweet Potato Skins are an American appetizer innovation that transforms the humble sweet potato into a vehicle for toppings. Sweet potatoes, indigenous to the Americas for over 5,000 years, were adopted into American cuisine and elevated through creative preparations like this crowd-pleasing dish.' WHERE slug = 'loaded-sweet-potato-skins-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Mac and Cheese Bites represent the American love affair with macaroni and cheese, which Thomas Jefferson reportedly brought back from Italy in the 1780s. These bite-sized, breaded, and fried versions emerged as a popular appetizer and party food in American restaurants and homes.' WHERE slug = 'mac-cheese-bites-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Mini Sliders are a quintessentially American creation, with the original slider attributed to White Castle in 1921. These miniature hamburgers transformed American dining culture and became a staple of sports bars and casual restaurants. The name "slider" comes from their small size that lets them "slide" right down.' WHERE slug = 'mini-sliders-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Oceania', history = 'Vegemite on Toast is Australia''s most iconic food, made from the spread created in 1922 by Cyril Callister using leftover brewer''s yeast. Vegemite became a symbol of Australian identity, featured in the classic jingle "Happy Little Vegemites." Spread thinly on buttered toast, it''s the quintessential Aussie breakfast.' WHERE slug = 'vegemite-au';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'South America', history = 'Pepperpot is Guyana''s national dish, a rich stew made with cassareep (a thick sauce from cassava root), meat, and spices. This Amerindian dish has been made in Guyana for centuries, with the unique property that it can be continuously replenished and reheated, with some pots reportedly being decades old.' WHERE slug = 'pepperpot';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Jalapeño Poppers are an American appetizer that celebrates the Mexican jalapeño pepper. The concept of stuffing and frying peppers has Mexican roots (chiles rellenos), but the cream cheese-stuffed, breaded version is a distinctly American bar food invention that became popular in the 1990s.' WHERE slug = 'jalapeno-poppers-mx';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Lebanese Falafel Wrap combines ancient Middle Eastern falafel with modern street food convenience. Falafel has been made in the Levant for thousands of years, originally from fava beans in Egypt. The wrap format reflects the global street food revolution and Lebanon''s vibrant food culture.' WHERE slug = 'lebanese-falafel-wrap-lb';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Global', history = 'Cloud Bread went viral on TikTok in 2020, a fluffy, colorful bread made from egg whites, sugar, and cornstarch. While it has roots in oopsie bread (a low-carb bread alternative from the Atkins diet era), the viral version emphasized visual appeal and became a symbol of pandemic-era home baking trends.' WHERE slug = 'cloud-bread';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Global', history = 'Crispy Pancakes became a TikTok sensation, showcasing the viral food trend of achieving ultra-crispy edges on classic pancakes through techniques like higher heat and butter basting. This trend represents how social media has democratized cooking techniques and created new food aesthetics.' WHERE slug = 'crispy-pancakes-tiktok';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'The Smash Burger technique gained massive popularity through social media in the 2020s, though the concept dates back to early American diners. By smashing a ball of beef on a screaming-hot griddle, the Maillard reaction creates an intensely flavorful crust. This technique has become the gold standard of burger preparation.' WHERE slug = 'smash-burger-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Kung Pao Cauliflower is a vegetarian adaptation of Kung Pao Chicken, a classic Sichuan dish named after Ding Baozhen, a Qing Dynasty governor (kung pao means "palace guardian"). The original recipe dates to the 19th century, and this modern plant-based version reflects China''s growing health-conscious dining trends.' WHERE slug = 'kung-pao-cauliflower-cn';
